*.json
# The shared engine-parity vectors ARE source (both engines' contract) —
# exempt them from the blanket *.json ignore.
!polariNoCode/parity_vectors/*.json
# The module register IS source (mp-1/mp-2: what exists, what is
# downloaded, where each sub-project repo lives) — a fresh clone
# without it loses the waves/requires/repo config.
!modules/polari-modules.json
# module data convention: committed initial data (plain JSON, small)
!modules/*/initialData/*.json
# …at any depth: computelod keeps its flow reports under initialData/lod1..4/, tensormath under
# initialData/fpga/ — the one-level rule silently left them out of every commit until 2026-09-26 (lod-3d)
!modules/*/initialData/**/*.json
# the app manifest IS source (sap: one polari-app.json replaces the hand-
# threaded core tables; carries the hand-tuned security stanza) — a fresh
# clone without it cannot admit the module or run `pol project`.
!modules/*/polari-app.json
# hwmap's selftest needs the mapping rules exercised against a REAL captured
# snapshot, not only synthetic ones — tracked SANITISED (hostname/MAC/by-id
# serials replaced; vendor:product ids, bus topology, IOMMU groups and driver
# names are not personal and stay real). See modules/hwmap/README.md.
!modules/hwmap/custom/fixture_pol_core.json
# cmod-0: the CONFORMED C manifest IS source like polari-app.json (derived by `pol cmod conform`, committed beside the
# project's Makefile), and the register snapshot the parser reads (derived from avr-libc's <avr/io.h>, carries its sha)
!modules/**/polari-firmware.json
!modules/cmod/custom/registers_*.json
# cmod-1: a graph's glue-build record (the rendered files' shas, the cost estimate, make alone, the twin equivalence proof) IS
# source — the CGlueBuild row is seeded from it
!modules/cmod/custom/glue_builds/*.json
# brd-bo: the board object's dev-hn-0 baseline (the byte-identity fixture) and the ingested Zephyr files' provenance ARE source
!modules/board/custom/fixtures/*.json
!modules/board/custom/upstream/**/SOURCE.json
# brd-fi/ucd-0e1: pinned offline wire-contract snapshots (custom/contracts/<class>.v<N>.json) ARE source — what a
# fresh server generates, the installer's compat fallback with no live exposure. Without this exemption the blanket
# *.json ignore silently drops them (the same gap the others above fix; UnoAnalogState.v1.json/SimRigState.v2.json
# were only in git via a force-add that never closed it)
!modules/board/custom/contracts/*.json
# pcb-0: the ingested ecc83-pp demo's provenance (package/version/licence, per-file sha256) IS source, same reason as board's —
# without this exemption the blanket *.json ignore silently drops it on every commit (the gap this line fixes)
!modules/pcb/custom/upstream/**/SOURCE.json
*.pyc
*.db
*/falcon
*__pycache__
testDoc.txt
testDocOne.txt
testDocTwo.txt
data/
# Claude Code local files (settings, memory) — keep private
.claude/
CLAUDE.local.md
# acct-0: matrix run reports are artifacts, not source
test-results/
# the board module's work dir (test probes' POLARI_BOARD_HOME default when run
# from the framework root instead of a tmp dir; the real module default is
# already ~/.cache/polari-board) — never source, ignore it here too
board-home/

# ============================================================
# Binary artifacts — no build artifacts in git
# ============================================================
# They are large, they change on every rebuild, and git keeps every
# version forever. Each gets a fetch-or-build path instead: the
# FreeType tarball is now downloaded (checksum-gated, several mirrors)
# by the Dockerfile rather than vendored here.
freetype/*.tar.gz
*.qcow2
*.img
*.img.gz
*.iso
*.deb
*.apk
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
